SF0098HS001/ADOPTED
Page 1-line 3 After "ballots;" insert "making conforming amendments;
repealing an obsolete provision;".
Page 2-line 1 After "affiliated." insert "If the candidate for school
board trustee is registered to vote during the period
when changes in party affiliation are prohibited under
W.S. 22-5-214(a) during the year of the general
election, the candidate's party affiliation shall be
the party that the candidate was affiliated with at the
time changes in party affiliation were prohibited. If

the candidate for school board trustee was not
registered to vote during the period when declarations
or changes in party affiliation are prohibited under
W.S. 22-5-214(a) during the year of the general
election, then the candidate's party affiliation shall
be the party that the candidate declared when the
candidate filed his application for election under W.S.
22-22-202.".
Page 2-line 4 Delete entirely and insert:
"Section 2. W.S. 22-6-117(a) by creating a new paragraph (xii), 22-6-123,
22-22-202(a) and by creating a new subsection (c) are amended to read:
22-6-117. Order of listing offices in partisan elections.
(a) The major party primary and general partisan election ballots shall
contain the offices to be voted on in the following order:
(xii) Candidates for school board trustees.".
Page 2-after line 16 Insert:
"22-22-202. Filing of application; form.
(a) A qualified elector may be nominated for the office of school
district trustee or member of a community college board by filing an application
for election in the office of the county clerk not more than ninety (90) nor
less than seventy (70) days prior to the election. The application shall be in
substantially the following form:
APPLICATION FOR ELECTION FOR SCHOOL OR
COMMUNITY COLLEGE TRUSTEE
I, the undersigned, swear or affirm that I was born on ...., ....(year), and
that I have been a resident of the State of Wyoming since ...., and that I am
a registered voter of the .... school district or community college district
(and resident of trustee residence area or subdistrict ...., if any), and that
I am registered as a member of ...., party, residing at ...., and I do hereby
request that my name, ...., be printed on the ballot of the election to be held
on the .... day of ...., ....(year), as a candidate for the office of .... for
a term of .... years. I hereby declare that if I am elected, I will qualify for
the office.
Dated: ....
.......... (Signature of Candidate)
.... Name as it is to appear on the ballot
(c) A qualified elector may be nominated for the office of community
college trustee by filing an application for election in the office of the
county clerk not more than ninety (90) nor less than seventy (70) days prior to
the election. The application shall be in substantially the following form:
APPLICATION FOR ELECTION FOR COMMUNITY COLLEGE TRUSTEE

I, the undersigned, swear or affirm that I was born on ...., ....(year), and
that I have been a resident of the State of Wyoming since ...., and that I am
a registered voter of the .... community college district (and resident of
subdistrict ...., if any), residing at ...., and I do hereby request that my
name, ...., be printed on the ballot of the election to be held on the .... day
of ...., ....(year), as a candidate for the office of .... for a term of ....
years. I hereby declare that if I am elected, I will qualify for the office.
Dated: ....
.......... (Signature of Candidate)
.... Name as it is to appear on the ballot
Section 3. W.S. 22-6-125(a)(viii) is repealed.".
Page 2-line 18 Delete "Section 3." and insert "Section 4.".
KNAPP, CHAIRMAN
SF0098HW001/ADOPTED
Page 2-line 1 After "affiliated" insert ", if any". In the House
standing committee amendment (SF0069HS001/A) to this
line, after "W.S. 22-22-202." insert "Any candidate who
is registered as an independent and who is not
affiliated with any party at the time they file their
nominating petition shall be listed on the ballot as an
independent candidate.". CHESTEK
